// Title: Potential Persistence Via TypedPaths
// Sigma ID: 086ae989-9ca6-4fe7-895a-759c5544f247
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-22 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects modification addition to the 'TypedPaths' key in the user or admin registry from a non
//   standard application. Which might indicate persistence attempt
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/dez_/status/1560101453150257154
//   - https://forensafe.com/blogs/typedpaths.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_typed_paths.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\TypedPaths.*$" and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\explorer.exe"))))
